  "comment": "Manifest for one atomic knowledge release. The verified plane is an Open Knowledge Format (OKF v0.2) markdown bundle rooted at bootstrap/; 'packs' pins EVERY file in the bundle (concept .md files and the reserved index.md/log.md alike) by sha256+size so no file can be altered without changing the manifest, and the manifest is what the release workflow attests (Sigstore build provenance). knowledge_verify rejects any undeclared file. 'version' is monotonic; a client rejects any manifest whose version is <= the highest version it has already trusted (anti-rollback). 'prev_digest' chains to the previous manifest. In the in-package bootstrap snapshot there is no attestation: it is trusted because it rode in on the SSH-signed skill release.",
